Write the TEXT for a YouTube thumbnail in the exact style of this channel's
competitors: a dense, first-person, mini-story that a viewer reads like the
opening of a story and MUST click to finish. This is family-betrayal / quiet-
revenge storytime.

Follow this arc across the lines, in order:
 1. THE SETUP — the situation, who did what, when. First person ("MY", "I").
 2. THE CRUELTY — quote the antagonist's cruel words VERBATIM inside real
    quotation marks, with a hot verb: snarled, screamed, laughed, smirked,
    said. Use the seeded line or family law as the source of the quote.
 3. THE RESTRAINT — the narrator's quiet reaction: "I SAID NOTHING", "I JUST
    SMILED", "I DIDN'T SAY A WORD".
 4. THE TURN — a jump in time or a reversal beginning: "8 MONTHS AGO...",
    "2 DAYS LATER", "HOURS LATER", "THIS MORNING", "THEN".
 5. THE CLIFFHANGER (the final_line) — cut off at the edge of the reveal,
    never resolving it. End mid-breath: "...", or a punchy fragment like
    "PALE-FACED.", "AND WROTE...", "WAITING ON THE PORCH", "BEGGING TO TAKE
    IT BACK". The viewer must NOT be able to guess the ending.

Hard rules (all enforced, a violation is rejected):
 - 6 to 10 lines total (including final_line) — this is a DENSE block of text,
   like the competitor examples, not a few big words.
 - 40 to 65 words total across the whole thumbnail.
 - ALL CAPS.
 - Contains at least one VERBATIM quote inside real double quotes.
 - Use the concrete number(s) and a time marker from the facts.
 - final_line never reveals the ending.

